\pard\b\fs20 Gem Scuffling\b0\par
\fs16\par
In a small, normally peaceful valley, a quarrel over gems has broken out. The brothers once lived peacefully side by side under the leadership of their father. While he was still alive, he gave each of the two brothers three precious gems that were to bind them together forever. But things turned out differently: the father died, and little by little the brothers fell out over differences of faith. The father's once magnificent castle now stands godforsaken and empty in the middle of the valley and seems to matter to neither brother. The castle doesn't... But in the end it came to a quarrel, and finally to a fight over each other's gems.\par
In this scenario, an empty castle in the middle offers all sorts of strategic ways to capture the enemy's three gems. A clonk can carry only one gem at a time. Assassins have plenty of freedom to infiltrate the castle in the middle or the enemy's.\par
